flow "Sidecar service mesh"
summary "Co-located proxies handle mTLS encryption, identity, and traffic policies transparently, unless layered retries trigger a retry storm."
tags service-mesh networking microservices
level intermediate
source "https://istio.io/latest/docs/ops/deployment/architecture/"
related distributed-systems/circuit-breaker distributed-systems/retry-backoff-dlq

node cp "Control Plane" service
group pod-a "Pod A"
node app-a "Orders App" service in=pod-a
node proxy-a "Sidecar A" service in=pod-a tone=primary
group pod-b "Pod B"
node proxy-b "Sidecar B" service in=pod-b
node app-b "Payments App" service in=pod-b
edge cp > proxy-a dashed
edge cp > proxy-b dashed
edge app-a > proxy-a
edge proxy-a > proxy-b
edge proxy-b > app-b

scenario mtls-route "Transparent mTLS and routing via sidecars"
  step config "Control plane pushes certs and policy"
    "The control plane issues short-lived workload certificates and routing rules to both sidecars. Application code stays free of TLS and retry libraries."
    detail "In Istio, the control plane (`istiod`) acts as a Certificate Authority issuing SPIFFE-compliant X.509 certificates tied to service accounts and converts high-level traffic policies into Envoy configurations pushed to the C++ sidecar proxies at runtime."
    send cp > proxy-a "SPIFFE cert + routes"
    send cp > proxy-b "SPIFFE cert + policy" with
    state cp,proxy-a,proxy-b active
  step mtls-call "Sidecars wrap plain traffic in mTLS"
    "Orders App calls `payments` over plain localhost HTTP. Sidecar A intercepts it, establishes **mutual TLS** with Sidecar B, verifies both identities, and Sidecar B forwards locally to Payments App."
    send app-a > proxy-a "HTTP /charge"
    send proxy-a > proxy-b "mTLS /charge"
    send proxy-b > app-b "HTTP /charge"
    state app-a,proxy-a,proxy-b,app-b success
    callout proxy-a "mTLS + telemetry transparent to app"

scenario retry-storm "Misconfigured retries amplify into a storm" from=mtls-route/mtls-call
  step slow-b "Payments App degrades and times out"
    "Payments App slows down past the 500ms timeout. If both the app SDK and Sidecar A (and upstream gateways) each retry 3 times, load multiplies exponentially."
    state app-b error
    effect app-b shake
    send proxy-b > proxy-a "504 Timeout"
  step amplify "Layered retries flood Payments"
    "Sidecar A fires 3 retries while Orders App also retries 3 times — turning 1 failing call into **9x traffic** and burying Payments under a **retry storm**."
    send app-a > proxy-a "3x app retries"
    send proxy-a > proxy-b "9x mesh retries!"
    state proxy-a,proxy-b error
    effect proxy-b shake
    callout proxy-b "9x load prevents recovery"
  step budget "Retry budget stops the amplification"
    "Enabling a **retry budget** (e.g., max 20% extra traffic) and disabling duplicate app-layer retries sheds excess retries so Payments can recover."
    detail "Envoy's `retryBudget` (configured via an Istio `DestinationRule`) defaults to `percent: 20` of active and pending requests with `minRetryConcurrency: 3`. Once concurrent retries exceed the budget, Envoy skips further retries so the struggling upstream can drain and recover."
    state proxy-a warning
    send cp > proxy-a "retry-budget=20%"
    callout proxy-a "Cap retries at one layer only"
